From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mio <mio@mio19.uk>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:01:22 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] raumata: enforce each stack's airtime share and accept advert
 coordinates

Background traffic stops once a protocol has used its hourly share. A MeshCore companion can set the position carried in adverts.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

diff --git a/docs/raumata-dual-protocol.md b/docs/raumata-dual-protocol.md
index 667f2f1991b3b345ea950c951e8634b396b9d478..b7352e7595e254906c60e0b0689c849402e6ca00 100644
--- a/docs/raumata-dual-protocol.md
+++ b/docs/raumata-dual-protocol.md
@@ -65,9 +65,11 @@ unmodified.
   and `sendingPacket`/`rawTxActive`/`isChannelBusy()`. `MeshCoreRadio` reports
   channel busy whenever Meshtastic is transmitting or actively receiving a LoRa
   frame, preventing TX-over-RX collisions.
-- **Airtime budget**: raw MeshCore transmissions are logged to Meshtastic's
-  `AirTime` tracker (`TX_LOG`), and `PresenceScheduler` scales the MeshCore
-  `Dispatcher` airtime budget factor to 25% of the regional duty cycle.
+- **Airtime budget**: each stack records its own transmit time. Background
+  traffic stops once that stack has used its mode share of the regional duty
+  cycle (10% for the secondary protocol, 50% when both are active, 90% for the
+  primary). Text, routing, and admin messages are still sent. Raw MeshCore
+  transmissions are also logged to Meshtastic's `AirTime` tracker.
 
 ## Dual identity, presence, and node features
 
@@ -81,7 +83,9 @@ implement a full `BaseChatMesh` companion node:
 - **Name Synchronization**: defaults to Meshtastic `owner.long_name` /
   `short_name` and tracks owner updates unless an explicit `raumata/mc_name`
   override is set via `CMD_SET_ADVERT_NAME`.
-- **Presence**: staggered boot announcements (`T+15s` MeshCore advert, `T+20s`
+- **Presence**: advert coordinates come from `CMD_SET_ADVERT_COORDS` when a
+  MeshCore companion has set them, otherwise from Meshtastic `localPosition`.
+  Staggered boot announcements (`T+15s` MeshCore advert, `T+20s`
   Meshtastic `NodeInfo`) and 15-minute periodic adverts with deterministic
   per-node jitter and GPS coordinates from `localPosition`.
 - **Persistence & Messaging**: up to 8 group channels (`raumata/mc_ch`) and 32
